[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) says it is one bug with one fix queued. Read report by report, it
is three problems with three different fixes. The queued parser fix closes only the first one.

<Callout kind="warn">
Not known. Three problems, one fix queued. Each problem now has its own ticket.
</Callout>

## What #4471 holds

<ProblemTable ticket={4471} />

## The three problems

**`parser` — the shared parser reads every date month first.** All our tenants write the day
first. A booking for 7 April becomes 4 July, through the app, by email and through the
booking-v2 form. The queued fix is for this one.

**`hint` — booking-v3 prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under its date field.** Only tenants on booking-v3
(Alder Physio, Copper Studio, Pale Harbour) and only reports through that form. People type
what the hint tells them, month first; the form then reads the date the tenant's way, day
first. The result looks the same as `parser`, so subject-line merging put it in #4471, but the
parser fix does not touch it. The fix is the hint (or reading the field the way it hints).

**`shift` — the date lands one day early.** Day and month are not swapped: Tuesday 12 May shows
as Monday 11 May, a client in Toronto gets Monday while Lisbon gets Tuesday, an invite arrives
before the booking was made. That is a date stored or sent as a midnight time and converted
across time zones. Neither code path in `causes.ts` produces it, so the cause table files these
under `parser` with a footnote.

## Why the merge hid them

- Merging by subject line ([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)) cannot see
  any of this: every problem arrives as "wrong day".
- Intake tags come from the reporter's browser, not the tenant. Many reports tagged `hint` are
  `parser`, and many `hint` reports were tagged `parser`; the table counts by tenant and form.
- The cause table on #4471 picks the biggest group as the ticket's cause and marks the rest
  "no ticket of its own". They have tickets now.

## What to do

- Keep #4471 for `parser` only; split `hint` and `shift` into the tickets above.
- Ship the parser fix, and check booking-v3 and the time-zone path separately: neither is fixed by it.

